  "result": "The regex now only matches the standalone `====` delimiter line (only `=` characters, optionally surrounded by tabs/spaces, on its own line), and no longer matches the `==` inside the base64 string, since that occurs mid-line inside `background-image: url(...)`.\n\nSummary of the fix in `src/generators/utils/parse.ts:146`:\n\n```js\nconst delimiterRegex = /\\s*={2,}\\s*/gm;\n```\n\u2192\n```js\nconst delimiterRegex = /^[ \\t]*={2,}[ \\t]*$/gm;\n```\n\nThis anchors the delimiter match to an entire line consisting only of `=` characters (with optional surrounding spaces/tabs), rather than any run of `==` anywhere in the text \u2014 which previously matched base64 padding like `...ErkJggg==') !important;`, causing corrupted `domainPatterns` entries and downstream `Invalid regular expression` crashes.\n\nBoth the config tests (`tests/config/jest.config.js`) and the parse-specific tests (`tests/generators/utils/jest.config.js`) pass with this change.",
